{
  "id": "27667_danpan",
  "headword": "{談判|だんぱん}",
  "reading": "だんぱん",
  "romaji": "danpan",
  "part_of_speech": "noun, suru verb",
  "gloss": "negotiation; bargaining; talks",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "negotiation; bargaining; talks",
      "explanation": "Direct negotiation or confrontation between parties to settle a dispute or press a demand, often a forceful face-to-face discussion."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "27667_danpan_ex1",
      "japanese": "{直接|ちょくせつ}{談判|だんぱん}する。",
      "english": "To negotiate directly.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "27667_danpan_ex2",
      "japanese": "{値段|ねだん}について{店|みせ}と{談判|だんぱん}した。",
      "english": "I bargained with the shop over the price.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "27667_danpan_ex3",
      "japanese": "{社長|しゃちょう}に{直接|ちょくせつ}{談判|だんぱん}して{給料|きゅうりょう}を{上|あ}げてもらった。",
      "english": "I confronted the company president directly and got my salary raised.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Refers to negotiating face to face, often to press a demand or settle a dispute. It carries a more forceful, confrontational nuance than ordinary {交渉|こうしょう}. Takes する.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {直接|ちょくせつ}{談判|だんぱん}: direct negotiation; confronting someone in person\n- {談判|だんぱん}に{行|い}く: to go to negotiate or press a demand\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {交渉|こうしょう}: negotiation — the neutral, standard term, including formal business and diplomacy\n- {掛|か}け{合|あ}う: to negotiate with; take a matter up with — a more colloquial verb",
